    "question": {
      ":question/id": "23f166c1-56c3-5031-87a3-50a36ff771bf",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "Find the value of ${x}_{1}-{x}_{2}$ given that $7a+4x=b$ and\n\n$$\na=\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix},\\,x=\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{4}\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ -30 \\\\ 42 \\\\ -42\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Using the properties of addition/subtraction and scalar multiplication of vectors to isolate $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7a+4x & =b \\\\ 4x & =b-7a \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{4}(b-7a) \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{4}(\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ -30 \\\\ 42 \\\\ -42\\end{bmatrix}-7\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix}) \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{4}\\begin{bmatrix}-36 \\\\ 12 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ x & =\\begin{bmatrix}-9 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=-9-3=-12.$",
